{"id":21519,"date":"2022-08-09T10:52:00","date_gmt":"2022-08-09T15:52:00","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/womgroup.com\/?post_type=news_item&#038;p=21519"},"modified":"2022-09-14T15:43:28","modified_gmt":"2022-09-14T20:43:28","slug":"wom-secures-iso-45001-certification","status":"publish","type":"news_item","link":"https:\/\/womgroup.com\/news_item\/wom-secures-iso-45001-certification\/","title":{"rendered":"WOM Secures ISO 45001:2018 Recertification"},"content":{"rendered":"\t\t<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"21519\" class=\"elementor elementor-21519\" data-elementor-post-type=\"news_item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<section class=\"elementor-section elementor-top-section elementor-element elementor-element-7e8a525 elementor-section-boxed elementor-section-height-default elementor-section-height-default\" data-id=\"7e8a525\" data-element_type=\"section\" data-e-type=\"section\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-container elementor-column-gap-default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-column elementor-col-100 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-7931673\" data-id=\"7931673\" data-element_type=\"column\" data-e-type=\"column\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-4369333 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"4369333\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><em><strong>Recertification helps further protect employees and visitors from work-related incidents<\/strong><\/em><\/p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">HOUSTON, TX, August 9, 2022 &#8211; &#8211; Worldwide Oilfield Machine (\u201cWOM\u201d) today announced it has successfully earned ISO 45001:2018 recertification for its Canemont location.\u00a0 WOM earned this distinction after completing multiple audits conducted by a third-party certifying body.\u00a0<\/p><blockquote><p>\u201cAchieving ISO 45001:2018 certification highlights our commitment to our employees, community and customers, by continuously evaluating and improving our safety processes to ensure we exceed the highest standards possible,\u201d said <strong>Rani Puranik, Executive Vice President and Chief Financial Officer<\/strong>. \u201cWOM owes this recognition to the dedication of our employees and safety leaders who continue to push the company forward, with their participation and commitment. Our WOM employee partners not only want our company to be known as a world-class manufacturer, but an industry role model, advocating for innovation in safety, sustainability, and quality.\u201d<\/p><\/blockquote><p style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">ISO 45001 is\u00a0the world\u2019s\u00a0international standard for occupational health and safety. This certification is issued to protect employees and visitors from work-related accidents and diseases.\u00a0ISO 45001 certification was developed to mitigate any factors that can cause employees and businesses irreparable harm. Its standards originate through a committee of health and safety management experts who looked closely at multiple approaches to system management, including ISO 9001 and ISO 14001. The ISO 45001 standard was designed to take other existing occupational health and safety standards, such as OHSAS 18001, into account, as well as the ILO\u2019s labor standards, conventions and safety guidelines.<\/span><\/p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">WOM\u2019s ISO 45001:2018, ISO 9001:2015, and ISO 14001:2015 certifications require comprehensive audits by internal teams and validation by a third-party certifying body to ensure conformance with the standard. Visit <a href=\"https:\/\/womgroup.com\/certifications\">https:\/\/womgroup.com\/certifications<\/a> to view all current WOM certifications and standards.<\/p><p><em># # #<\/em><\/p><p style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>About ISO<br \/><\/strong>ISO (International Organization for Standardization) is the world\u2019s largest developer and publisher of International Standards. ISO is a network of national standards bodies of 167\u00a0countries, with a Central Secretariat in Geneva, Switzerland.<\/p><p style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>About WOM<br \/><\/strong>Worldwide Oilfield Machine provides premium flow control and pressure containment systems to the upstream and midstream oil and gas sector. Our vertically integrated, employee-driven company headquartered in Houston, Texas exists to partner with relevant stakeholders in local communities in which we operate, delivering reliable, innovative, cost-efficient, and climate-conscious solutions to our customer\u2019s business needs. We strive for a larger purpose, dedicating our resources to building sustainable ecosystems in local communities for future generations in two ways\u2014using an ESG-focused product life cycle for our customers within the industries we serve, and supporting school systems to career paths within local education. We leverage our experience and knowledge of business processes and technology, along with healthy investment in human and monetary capital to systemically improve the quality of life for the people in our global communities.<\/p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Our WOM group of companies employ 4,000 employees across 13 strategically located global facilities.\u00a0Our diversified workforce supports manufacturing facilities, engineering centers, sales offices, and assembly and testing locations across 10 countries.<\/p>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/section>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Recertification helps further protect employees and visitors from work-related incidents HOUSTON, TX, August 9, 2022 &#8211; &#8211; Worldwide Oilfield Machine (\u201cWOM